INT. CHURCH BASEMENT - ROLLER DERBY LOCKER ROOM - NIGHT

Folding chairs. A Sunday-school felt board still reading LOVE THY NEIGHBOUR. Five women lace skates under a flickering bulb.

TAMSIN FAIRWEATHER, thirties, captain, tapes her wrist. NANA OKONKWO, twenties, jammer, bounces a knee. ROSA ESPINOZA, forties, blocker, eats a banana. KIT HALVORSEN, nineteen, rookie, stares at her laces. YUKI TANABE, thirties, ref in stripes, sits apart with a clipboard.

TAMSIN
Kit, you're good?

KIT
Fine.

NANA
She's not fine. She's looking at her shoes.

ROSA
Leave her, Nana.

NANA
I'm just saying. First bout.

Kit pulls a lace tight. Snaps it.

KIT
It's a church basement. How scary can it be?

YUKI
Last month somebody lost a tooth in the nave.

Silence. Rosa chews her banana.

TAMSIN
Alright, listen. Keep your heads up and your elbows in. No heroics.

NANA
No heroics.

ROSA
(deadpan)
Some heroics.

Tamsin grins. Stands. The felt board rattles on its easel.

TAMSIN
Let's go.
